  "description": "Tesla looks bullish + Position Sizing and Stops",
  "body_html": "<p>If you already know about position sizing and stops, you can <strong>see the stock I bought more of,</strong> either down below or in the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/a27b2288-ae6c-4cb6-833a-bfb84d676813?target_reply_id=ec327594-4e6a-4815-9676-3316456938fd&amp;showTarget=true\">Quick Notes</a> where I put out updates. </p><p>I kept this article simple, but really try to digest it. Read it twice if you have to. And as always, if you have questions, tag me in the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/7d6043ce-5d9e-4c0f-bac6-78e3f9c8ef3c\">Main Chat</a>, happy to answer questions. </p><p>Position sizing and stops is one of the most common questions I get. It is also one of the hardest to answer, simply because so many variables go into the answer, for you, individually. Some examples include, but are not limited to:</p><ol><li><p>What timeframe are you trading?</p><ol><li><p>Your stop/position will be different if trading a daily chart timeframe vs. a monthly chart timeframe.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>What is the normal volatility of the asset you are trading?</p><ol><li><p>Does the asset have a lot of public interest, and thus moves more?</p></li></ol></li><li><p>What is the market cap of the asset you are investing in?</p><ol><li><p>A penny stock obviously is going to move significantly more than a blue chip stock in a single day. You can’t have the same stop strategy for both. </p></li></ol></li></ol><p>Last year, I was predominantly mid-term trading (weeks/months). This year, due to the incredibly volatile news and my life getting busy with kids, the homestead and a new puppy I am training…I am long term trading (months+). Note, I say “long term trading”…not “investing”. Just because I am using a longer timeframe, does not mean I will hold a position forever, or not cut a bad position that went against my initial speculation. We also never let a profit turn to a bag. Never. </p><h4><strong>We accept risk </strong><em><strong>at the beginning</strong></em><strong> of a trade…not later! </strong></h4><p><strong>Don’t let a “bad” position turn into “horrific” position! This is what destroys many retail, holding onto losing positions too long. (And not holding their winners long enough!)</strong></p><h4>To keep this simple, we will just use a portfolio of $100,000 and a ticker most people are familiar with, Tesla, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$TSLA&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>. </h4><p>If you were to ask me where to put a stop for TSLA, the first thing I would ask you is: <strong>“What timeframe are you trading?”</strong> Depending on your answer, I would give a response of $337.25 or $214.25. The $337.25 would derive from you saying “I am trading the daily timeframe” and the $214.25 would be produced if you said “I am trading the monthly timeframe”.  </p><p> Lets walk through those 2 different responses. </p><p>If you said “monthly”, naturally I would pull up the monthly chart. I then ask myself: <strong>“Where would the price have to be, for me to say ‘the upward trend has potentially shifted down?’”</strong> The answer is very simple…if we start making new lows, even locally, then clearly something has changed and the trade is most likely (not always) negated. Large drawdowns, and even bear markets, most often will start with local lows, and then transition into those devastating drops. </p><p>Look at the monthly Tesla chart below (which TSLA has a volatility contraction pattern [bullish] on it btw. VCPs are what I trade &gt;95% of the time.) The process is simple…where would price action create a new local low? I plot out where the bulls stepped in, with volume, and see where the last price point they stepped in was at. That answer comes to $214.25. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png\" width=\"1345\" height=\"821\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:821,&quot;width&quot;:1345,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:189816,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196656956?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!V-pf!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e4f1cf5-5a0a-4b39-b7f8-c54a97dc8c42_1345x821.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><strong>“But Timothy! If I buy Tesla at $391.64 right now, and it drops to $214.25…that’s nearly a -40% loss!” </strong></p><p>You are correct! And that is where <strong>position sizing</strong> comes in. If you put all $100,000 into Tesla, and your bullish speculation is incorrect, your portfolio would lose $40,000. By reducing our initial position size, we can more effectively manage the damage a individual position does to our overall portfolio. </p><p>This is a personal rule…adjust for yourself…but I never let a single position risk more than -2% to -3% of my total portfolio equity. 3% of $100,000 means we are willing to risk $3000. </p><p>To make this even simpler for you, I have a free <a href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/v/G4JKzejz/\">StockTok Portfolio Risk Assessment</a> tool for TradingView, that does the math for you. From the example below, if we put $20,000 into Tesla, and take the full -40% risk, that is still Too Risky (greater than -3% risk to total portfolio equity). </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png\" width=\"837\" height=\"399\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:399,&quot;width&quot;:837,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:175856,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196656956?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HB8O!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2678dc00-ad1f-4a76-b406-cea84455bd63_837x399.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Putting $20,000 of your $100,000 into TSLA, with a -40% risk to the position is TOO RISKY to your total portfolio equity. </figcaption></figure></div><p>To reduce this portfolio equity risk, we must either:</p><ol><li><p>Reduce Position Amount</p></li><li><p>Reduce Position Risk</p></li><li><p>Reduce both Position Amount and Position Risk</p></li></ol><p>Because we want the full breadth of the chart, as in, not getting stopped out early, our best choice is to reduce position size. We want the flexibility to take a -39% move and not get stopped out early. In the image below, you can see that starting with $7000 would be moderate risk (-2.8%), and by dropping the initial position down to $5000 drops the portfolio risk to -2%, a much safer alternative. This is most often why when we occasionally have a position go against us, I can see people panicking…they are over positioned in an asset. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png\" width=\"792\" height=\"354\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:354,&quot;width&quot;:792,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:161350,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196656956?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wn_V!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffe78a28d-58fe-405c-a877-49dd280e0955_792x354.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Adjust position amount and/or position risk to reduce portfolio equity risk</figcaption></figure></div><p><strong>”But Timothy! If the stock goes up, I would have made way more money by putting in half my portfolio!”</strong></p><p>Well no shit lol. But that is only easy <em><strong>in hindsight</strong></em>. You may get away with it a few times, dumping your portfolio into a stock. But unforeseen events do happen.  I have seen many portfolios perish, eventually, with that bad habit. Be disciplined and consistent. </p><p>Just because we start small, does not mean we can’t or won’t have a large position. We can dollar cost average UP. Last year I bought Roblox 3 times over several weeks, totaling over $40k and compounding the 61% gain. Bull markets do not last a single day…you usually have a lot of time on your hands. If and when Tesla goes up, we can add to the position over time, compounding our winners. We begin risking profits, instead of initial portfolio equity. This article is about stops and position sizing, if you would like to learn more about DCA UP, read this article: <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/losers-dollar-cost-average-down\">How to Dollar Cost Average Up</a>.</p><p>Real briefly, to cover the $337.25 stop answer for Tesla, for someone trading shorter term (days). When I look at the daily chart, I ask myself the same question: “When would we be getting a new local low. That answer comes to $337.25. We do not want to be a bull, when new local lower lows are forming. Period. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png\" width=\"1388\" height=\"830\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:830,&quot;width&quot;:1388,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:233087,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196656956?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!poa_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8c500c0d-25c2-40dd-8d6d-6e43256d5ffb_1388x830.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Notice the local low for a daily chart will be different than a local low for a monthly chart, hence the $337.25</figcaption></figure></div><p>I also mentioned market cap size and volatility above, as that will tie into how you position a stop. How you position a stop or adjust position size for a stock, say like Nvidia vs. a smaller mid-cap stock, say like TeraWulf, is going to be different. The yellow boxes below show November 2024 to April 2025, which was largely a down period for most assets. During the same period, Nvidia with a market cap of $4.99T dropped -43%, whereas Wulf dropped -78%. Smaller market cap stocks, normally, will drop (and rise), significantly more. Wider stops and or smaller initial positions are often critical with these. But the rules and processes for estimating your stops are still the same as described above, where I use local lows. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png\" width=\"1437\" height=\"817\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:817,&quot;width&quot;:1437,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:216915,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/196656956?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!R3rY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6752df2f-eada-45c7-ac66-e1ba45d114c0_1437x817.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Same time period…but very different market caps, resulting in very different % changes.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Is the above methodology perfect? No. </p><h3>There is no perfect stop strategy. </h3><p>You will get stopped out sometimes. You will get annoyed or frustrated. But by being consistent, you will prevent your portfolio from going into the dumpster fire, that wipes out millions of retail investors every bear market or large drawdown. You are saving yourself, before the unexpected carnage hits. </p><p>If you find yourself getting stopped out too often, then that indicates your stock picking or strategy are not working, and that you either:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Need to take a break.</strong> </p><ol><li><p>Sometimes even my strategy is not “optimal” and I sit on the sidelines until I notice my strategy is working for me. I’m confident in my strategy long term, over time, but recognize that it will not work every single day. I sat out March and April, simply because the strategy was not working. It is now, so I go heavy again. Scale in heavy when its working, scale out when its not.</p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Refine your strategy. </strong></p><ol><li><p>Getting a consistent profitable strategy does take some time and testing. But if you consistently keep losing, then your strategy sucks or stock picking sucks. Accept it, refine it, and repeat until you find something that works. Lying to yourself will not improve your portfolio results. I know its a miserable process…but every successful trader must go through this. Sorry, not sorry.</p></li></ol></li></ol><p>Again, if you have questions, just ask me in the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/7d6043ce-5d9e-4c0f-bac6-78e3f9c8ef3c\">Main Chat</a>. I am available for you during market hours. </p><p>Don’t forget to like ❤️ and re-stack this please, its the only way we beat out the anonymous profiles and AI slop here on Substack.</p><h4><strong>Now, very briefly, the stock I am buying more of, to begin compounding one of our winners is… </strong></h4>",
